<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kiek in de Kök</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1470s</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kiek in de Kök is an artillery tower in the town wall of Tallinn (Reval), built from about 1475 and later heightened. Its Low German name, &quot;peep into the kitchen&quot;, came from the joke that from its upper floors the guards could see into the kitchens of the houses below. One of the strongest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> towers in the Baltic, it is now a museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kiek-in-de-kok.jpg" alt="Kiek in de Kök" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kiek_in_de_K%C3%B6k,_Tallin,_Estonia,_2012-08-05,_DD_02.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
